.TH "PB-TEAM-SCIM-SETUP" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-scim-setup - Open the WorkOS Admin Portal to connect your directory


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team scim setup <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print, and open in a browser where possible, a short-lived WorkOS Admin Portal link to connect your company directory with SCIM. Your IT admin follows the guide for your directory there. Once connected, Paperboat provisions members within seconds; map groups to roles with pb team scim map. The team needs enough seats.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for setup


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-scim(1)\fP
